.TH SCANF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
scanf \- read formatted input from standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B int scanf(const char *format);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads from
.BR stdin .
The compiler accepts additional destination pointer arguments.
Conversion specifications and stream behavior are described in
.BR fscanf (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of assignments, possibly zero. Returns EOF when input
fails before any conversion completes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fscanf (3crunch),
.BR fgetc (3crunch)
